In article <429efaa6-faf2-45c0-a804-0509a87e8bc0
@s9g2000prg.googlegroups.com>, JoaoSantos says...
> > > Else, if uswldtim == 0, we get the instadeath: tmp (the damage of
> > > the engulf attack) is set to the hero's HP. If the hero has half
> > > physical damage, double that, because at the end of gulpmu damage
> > > will be halved. This gives a message like "The purple worm totally
> > > digests you!"
> > Does this really count as instadeath?
> > You have one guaranteed turn to act. Everybody knows that being
> > swallowed by a monster is bad.
> I think it does. Sliming is also considered a (delayed) instadeath,
> and you can pray/use fire. Or stoning, also.
> The point is that you don't die by an enormous damage, but by
> a damage that's specifically (?) calculated for you to die.
> I'm not sure what's the "standard" definition of instadeath, so I may
> be wrong.

If you go by <http://www.steelypips.org/nethack/instadeath.html> it 
seems to fit well into the "delayed insta-death" category.

